WEBVTT

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.140
This is some kind of recording medium.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.210
It's an older type, but it's definitely that.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.680
Can you restore it?

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.480
I can try.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.520
There may be something we've never seen before on there.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.700
All right! Okay!

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.590
deai to wakare wo

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.590
On our long journey,

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.880
mune ni dakitomete susumou

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.880
let us remember the people we met and parted from

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.990
kioku wa itsumo yawaraka na tezawari de

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.990
Their memory always casts a gentle smile

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:26.200
hohoemikakete kureru

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:26.200
on the present day

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:33.630
sora no nioi to nami ga zawameku uta

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:33.630
I can smell the sky and hear the waves sing

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:39.760
nanigenai shiawase ga afuredashite

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:39.760
From this simple happiness

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.700
hajimari no yuuki mitsuketa

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.700
I derived my courage

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.690
mawaru yo mawaru yo

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.690
The world goes on

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.090
sekai wa mawaru yo

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.090
The world goes ever on

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.970
kokoro no hane hiroge

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:54.970
We spread the wings of our souls

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:59.780
bokura wa kyou wo ikiteyuku

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:59.780
and live our lives

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.980
tatoe donna kaze ga fuitemo

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.980
no matter what the times may bring

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.220
nandodemo jiyuu wo motomete

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.220
We will seek freedom

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.160
habataite yukou

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.160
like the birds

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:20.820
The Ocean Routes Stretch into the Distance

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:20.820
[ Part 2 ]

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.410
kanashimi wo norikoeta saki ni

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.410
We will find happiness

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:23.350
hikari ga aru kara

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:23.350
past whatever hardship there may be

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.240
For heaven's sake!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.000
You said you would show me around Gargantia!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.930
I never said that!

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.540
I've been way too busy lately.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.010
I don't have time for that crap!

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.880
How dare you speak to me like that?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.410
After we made vows to each other
about the future on that sea of flames!

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.470
I didn't vow anything!

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:47.810
Besides, I prefer gentle,
elegant ladies to tomboys like you!

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:49.940
Later!

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.020
Hold it right there!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.980
So if we remove this...

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.230
Loverboy!

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.280
Shaddup!

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.850
I'm getting something!

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:23.930
This is the first time one of our devices
has been able to read their data in detail!

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.390
Blueprints...

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.410
An operating manual?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.330
It's not for a Yunboro?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.630
This is state-of-the-art technology, closer to Chamber.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.640
I would guess...

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.210
this is a battle mech.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:46.200
The people who made this forged into space
and created the Galactic Alliance of Humankind.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.260
They escaped from a frozen Earth,

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.660
but they didn't stop fighting.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.160
It's sad, but it's true.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:56.420
We have to learn from their example.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.930
So that we don't go down the same path...

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.550
Sis!

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.560
Amy!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.270
Have you had lunch yet?

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:22.330
Huh. The Kugel fleet has quite the dining hall.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.320
Hey, why don't you relax a bit?

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.120
Well, we don't have this kind of food on Gargantia!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.290
That doesn't mean you can order the whole menu!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.960
I'll take responsibility.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.540
This is cool, isn't it?

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.010
Yeah.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.930
I ride this on excursions.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.410
You're really into those kinds
of machines, aren't you, Leema?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.500
I heard Pinion even tried to recruit you.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.560
Seriously?!

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:50.970
Uh...

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.350
At the time, it was just, uh...

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.310
You came to check out Chamber's cockpit, too.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.980
A-At that time, I was also, um...

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.200
And you saved Ledo with a submersible Yunboro!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.200
L-Let's not talk about that.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:10.660
Bevel!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.740
Are you okay?

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.080
Yeah. It's just that you guys make me laugh so hard...

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.160
Are you really all right?

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.680
Perfectly fine.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.210
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.140
There's more to come.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.590
Let's dig in!

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:29.950
That was delicious!

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.340
I'll be back!

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.310
You're gonna eat that much again?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.570
I can't run around or do strenuous
physical activity for any length of time.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:43.130
I've had a weak heart ever since I was born.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:47.360
And there's no way to treat it,
so all I can do is live with it as best I can.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.460
It must be tough.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:51.880
Nah. Not with my big sister around.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.040
Not to mention Dr. Ordum, Ledo, and everyone else.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.870
You're strong, Bevel.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.960
So are you, Leema.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:03.170
After all,

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.880
you've just started living in a place you knew nothing about,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.350
but you've already made friends and have a job.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.360
We're all weak, but we're all strong.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.850
Huh? Where's Leema?

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.910
She said she's going back
to her own ship for a while.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:31.200
She probably wants to do laundry or something.
The weather's right for it.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.570
Ah! Maybe I'll do mine too.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:51.170
All you have to do is capture the target
and abscond with him.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:52.550
Didn't I tell you before?

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:55.850
Our objective is to get Ledo to cooperate.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.120
How much power does Muzzle have locked away?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.360
Will we be able to control it?

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.050
There's still a lot we don't know.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.900
And if we don't get to the bottom of it,
we can't use it for battle.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.720
We need his knowledge.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.490
But coercion won't work with him.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.390
Still, there's no time.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:21.810
We've already failed at capturing Striker's pilot.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.710
I'm sure the homeland is tired of waiting.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:29.490
In that case, the pilot died,
which we couldn't have accounted for.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:34.600
We should thank our lucky stars that a new subject has appeared.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.640
I'll encourage Ledo to leave here himself.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.310
That doesn't change the plan.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:43.350
But if our nation turns its back on us, it's all over.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.480
For us and for this mech.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.440
Don't forget that.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.200
Report, please.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:04.580
It seems exhaustion among the residents is increasingly becoming a problem.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:08.280
We're still securing housing for people we took on from the Kugel fleet,

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.310
and ship repairs are still ongoing.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.360
We're also worried about lack of resources.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:18.570
We stocked up from those traders the other day,
but consumption is on the rise.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:20.250
It's only a matter of time.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.600
We haven't been able to get hold of
a few parts and batteries.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.400
Every guild is having difficulties.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.920
I thought this might happen.

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.610
Commodore, we need to deal
with these problems somehow.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:42.810
You should be able to get what you need here.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.400
I believe they also have rest facilities.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.540
I see.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.610
The Dragon Palace...

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:56.220
This is Commodore Ridget.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.930
I have an announcement for all residents.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:04.640
Gargantia is now setting course for the trading hub

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.610
known as the Dragon Palace.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.650
Hey, what's the Dragon Palace?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.320
What? You don't know?

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.010
This is great news!

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.280
To all captains and guildmasters:

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:22.290
please come up with a supply financing plan.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:27.210
Also, give careful consideration
to rewarding the efforts of your residents.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:33.170
Hey, there it is! The Dragon Palace!

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.950
That's it?!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.520
It's huge!

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.360
I'm amazed they managed
to get such a facility floating.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.530
Look! A pod of dolphins!

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.250
Yeah...

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.500
I've never seen them this close before.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.460
Come on, let's have fun!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.990
Yeah!

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.370
Bevel can't come?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:31.060
No.

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.300
It would be too much for him
to walk around a huge place like this.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.050
He said he's going to help
Dr. Ordum investigate something.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:40.430
That's too bad.

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:42.120
Let's buy him a souvenir.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:43.820
Good idea.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:50.010
Everyone, thank you for
submitting your proposals.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:53.120
I'll use these as the basis
for our trade negotiations.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.300
A fellow tradesman was telling me

00:10:55.580 --> 00:11:00.060
that the price of supplies made from iron is going up across the board right now.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:03.660
I heard somebody's buying up all the vegetable seeds and cereal.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:07.700
Then we'll get high prices
for the items we have to offer.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.750
In other words, the economy's good.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.860
Let's take advantage of it.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.000
Still, why now?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.190
Apparently,

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.280
it has something to do with Land's actions.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:20.910
Land?

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.210
Hey, is that...

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.240
For real?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.950
We'll be okay, right?

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.530
What does this mean?

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:33.210
Details are unknown, but some supplies are definitely being funneled to Land.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.130
Understood.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.670
We always need to be careful
about the doings of the Land nations.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:45.000
They may act unpredictably.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.210
When I meet with the top officials of the Dragon Palace,

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:50.140
I'll sound them out for confirmation.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.070
I see... Land...

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.000
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.530
I see. What shall we do, boss?

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:10.740
I wasn't interested in this amusement park,

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.980
but we'd best show caution and sniff around.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.300
Let's get ready.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.630
Aye, sir!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:20.460
What is this?!

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.260
It's like a festival, isn't it, Leema?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.430
Yes!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.380
Ledo! Wanna try that?

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:29.600
You take the gun,

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.920
and you shoot the prize you want.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.060
You use it like this.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.220
Go ahead.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:36.990
Whichever one you like.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:53.460
That was mean, Amy! You didn't prime the rifle!

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.130
What is this?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.450
Sorry about that!

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:02.560
Dolphins!

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.550
Yeah!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.590
There's so many of them!

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.940
Ledo, can you believe how many there are?

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:11.810
Yeah.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:14.200
Dolphins.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.480
Aquatic mammals.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:22.360
A species that sometimes comes to the surface
but has chosen to live in the sea.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.250
Why have they evolved like that?

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.570
When they return to the sea,

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.410
what is it they're living in pursuit of?

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.540
Hey, hey!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.370
You can play with the dolphins!

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:36.680
Really?

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:38.620
Play with dolphins?

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:40.340
Of course we're gonna do it!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.590
Do you have your swimsuit?

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.510
Swimsuit?

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:45.980
This! See?

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:49.250
You too, Amy?

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.390
Uh... yeah. Just in case.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.640
I can't just wear my underwear?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.590
Then let's go shopping first.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.510
That's totally you, Leema!

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.530
Yeah! I like it!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.250
Ledo, how about this one?

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.990
Yay!

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.500
Amy?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.080
Amy...

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.580
Hey, there are a lot more underwater!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.500
Dolphins?

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.410
I'm so jealous.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.640
Lucky...

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:14.760
Leema?

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.010
I-I mean...

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.730
You girls are so close.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.110
And I've never had this much fun before.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:26.820
Well, that's because you were in the Kugel fleet.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:33.570
Hey, Leema. Let us know if there's something you want to get off your chest.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.490
We're friends. Comrades.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:40.720
Thank you. But I'm fine.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:45.860
I was just thinking I wish I could've
played like that with my big brother.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:46.710
Sorry.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.880
You have a big brother?!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.170
What's he doing now?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.620
Where is he in the fleet?

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:52.180
Is he hot?

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:01.850
I believe we can get you all the supplies you need without any problems.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:03.760
I see.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:09.370
It's an honor to have the great Gargantia dock here.

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:13.780
You have much to sell,
and we made a good deal.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:14.570
Well, then...

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.170
Thank you.

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:20.040
You're welcome.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:27.530
I heard a rumor of favoritism
regarding the flow of some supplies.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:29.710
I'm relieved that my worrying was for nothing.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.190
This is the first I've heard of it.

00:16:32.190 --> 00:16:35.650
To us, every deal is precious.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.680
We don't play favorites.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.870
I know that now.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:40.980
That being said...

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:44.570
What's that?

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.530
The latest world map.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:50.400
It also reflects the distribution of power.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.300
Please take it.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.360
As a token of our friendship.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.820
Th-Thank you.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:03.040
Do you have plans after this?
We would like to host a dinner party for you.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.360
Ah... but...

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.990
That looks good! I bet he could use those to make all kinds of things.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:31.340
He'll love it, I'm sure.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:32.780
Then I'll get this.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.780
Hi! So you two are here?

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.110
You guys!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:38.320
Surprised to see you in this kinda shop.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.180
You got good taste.

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.620
It's to get a souvenir for Bevel. We were just about to leave.

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.060
I see.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:46.880
Well, you kids should be getting home, anyway.

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.980
From here on out, it's adult time.

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.840
Whatcha talkin' about, adult time?!

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:56.800
I better not catchu breachin' public order an' standards of decency!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.430
Ridget!

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:00.190
I'm on the clock!

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:04.770
Gotta keep patrollin' to make sure our residents don't cause trouble here at the Dragon Palace.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.310
They made her drink...

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.440
Let's just pretend we don't know her.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.710
Sheesh...

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:13.230
On the clock!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.970
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.600
I'll take her to her room.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:17.320
Okay.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.370
Hi!

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.370
Please excuse her.

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:21.530
Everyone, excuse us!

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:34.660
Oh, boy... What do you wanna do?

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:35.730
Just hang out?

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:38.520
"Local procurement," duh.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:39.470
Let's see...

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:59.100
Hey, miss.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:01.070
Sorry, but could you return what you stole?

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:05.790
I'm referring to my heart, of course.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:07.950
I'm gonna puke.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.540
You're truly a silly man.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:15.750
An angel!

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.620
Huh? Where's Leema?

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:27.380
Our nation is preparing to call us home.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:32.020
Unless we complete the mission by the time the squad gets here, it'll be called off.

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.460
That's ridiculous!

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.980
What, are they gonna dump Muzzle too?

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:40.820
Their top secret military weapon can't be allowed outside the country any longer.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:45.250
I'm sure that's what our superiors are thinking.

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:48.870
They're afraid of information leaking
to an enemy nation more than anything.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:52.560
Do something to keep them at bay.
Just for a little longer.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:10.550
What's this?

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.060
What is it?

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:16.690
A machine that communicates
based on autonomous analysis of words.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:18.530
Lost technology...

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.970
A talking machine...

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.470
Like Chamber?

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:27.100
Yeah. This probably worked along the
same lines as his artificial intelligence.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.240
They could actually make that...

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:35.210
Without that superior intellect, humans wouldn't have made it through the last ice age.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:37.010
Or so I believe.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:56.710
What did you want to show me?

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:02.400
That's...

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.380
A Yunboro?

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:09.270
No.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:11.790
The mech from those blueprints?!

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:18.790
Ledo, I want you to come to my country and help us research this machine.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:20.800
What?!

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.910
Dotoctang ino lavang bidy.{What did we do for this again?}

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:53.110
Muzzle, I may be exposing you to danger.

00:21:57.490 --> 00:22:00.150
Is that okay? Or not? Which one?

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:10.210
I'm sorry I can't understand how you feel.

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:15.600
I'm the only one who's operated you.

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.000
To live—to get stronger—

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.770
this was my only path.

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:25.010
And yet...

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:30.100
It's crazy, isn't it? To think that I...

00:22:30.610 --> 00:22:32.920
have started to hate the idea of fighting.

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:46.420
Good job!

00:22:47.070 --> 00:22:48.450
Amy!

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:51.140
What's wrong? You said you wanted to meet alone.

00:22:54.080 --> 00:22:54.950
Leema?

00:22:56.460 --> 00:22:57.600
I have a favor to ask!

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:02.000
I want you to convince Ledo...

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:04.520
to leave Gargantia.

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.300
Huh? I don't understand.

00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:07.350
What do you mean?

00:23:08.020 --> 00:23:10.230
Of course, you would go with him.

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:10.990
Bevel, too.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.500
Wait, I really don't understand!

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.800
Start from the beginning!

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:20.780
l want you, Ledo, and Bevel to come with me.

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:22.880
Come with you... where?

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:26.550
Where I was born. Land.

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:28.100
Land?!

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:30.260
You're from Land?

00:23:31.650 --> 00:23:35.100
If you go, I'm sure Ledo will too.

00:23:39.220 --> 00:23:40.230
What did Ledo say?

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:44.000
He wouldn't answer me.

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:47.340
But I bet it's because he can't leave you behind.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:49.710
That's what it looked like to me.

00:23:49.710 --> 00:23:50.710
So...

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:53.100
Then my answer is the same!

00:23:53.690 --> 00:23:55.450
I can't imagine leaving Gargantia!

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.150
Bevel...

00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:00.830
He may be able to be cured on Land!

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.630
Is that true?

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:09.880
I don't know.

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:13.690
She's the first person I've met from Land.

00:24:13.690 --> 00:24:16.900
We were always told it was a place not to get mixed up with.

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:20.100
l can't believe Leema's from there.

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:27.310
She said I could be with you, but just the thought of moving to an unknown place...

00:24:27.310 --> 00:24:30.820
But if Bevel can be cured, I...

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:33.700
And what if that's not true?

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:35.300
What if they can't cure him?!

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:37.280
We would just be putting him in danger!

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:44.780
What should we do?

00:24:44.780 --> 00:24:47.030
It's such a sudden decision to make.

00:24:47.030 --> 00:24:48.930
I don't know!

00:24:48.930 --> 00:24:50.020
Ledo...

00:25:41.850 --> 00:25:42.770
Commodore!

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:45.980
Another fleet approaching at four o'clock!

00:25:46.540 --> 00:25:48.010
Stay on guard!

00:25:48.010 --> 00:25:48.640
Yes, ma'am!

00:25:52.780 --> 00:25:54.720
Never seen that kind of ship before.

00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:55.590
Pirates?

00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:56.610
Unknown.

00:25:57.340 --> 00:25:59.150
I'll send out the escort ships.

00:25:59.150 --> 00:26:00.080
Please do.

00:26:00.080 --> 00:26:00.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:26:16.220 --> 00:26:18.930
I wasn't in time...

00:26:26.380 --> 00:26:28.460
So they're finally making a show of force!

00:26:28.460 --> 00:26:28.810
No.

00:26:29.530 --> 00:26:32.930
Showing up here without even contacting us

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:35.820
means they've given up on us
and the plan altogether.

00:26:35.820 --> 00:26:36.860
That can't be!

00:26:36.860 --> 00:26:38.400
But there's still something we can do.

00:26:38.400 --> 00:26:40.880
If we can just capture Ledo, we win.

00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:42.530
Forget Leema. Let's go!

00:26:44.810 --> 00:26:48.510
Approaching fleet, this is Gargantia!

00:26:48.510 --> 00:26:51.750
Inform us of your fleet designation and your intent!

00:26:52.250 --> 00:26:54.140
Commodore, who are they?

00:26:54.140 --> 00:26:56.270
They don't seem to be pirates.

00:26:56.270 --> 00:26:59.770
They've been keeping pace with us.

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:01.770
Commodore...

00:27:02.400 --> 00:27:03.350
This is Ridget.

00:27:04.200 --> 00:27:07.310
None of those ships have interlocks.

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:10.520
Warships...

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:11.820
Bellows!

00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:12.480
What are they?!

00:27:12.480 --> 00:27:13.810
I don't know!

00:27:13.810 --> 00:27:14.590
Ledo!

00:27:15.950 --> 00:27:18.360
Leema, do you know something about this?

00:27:18.360 --> 00:27:20.420
What is that approaching fleet?!

00:27:20.420 --> 00:27:22.700
It's a special forces armada from Land.

00:27:22.900 --> 00:27:23.920
Land?!

00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:25.330
Who are you?!

00:27:25.330 --> 00:27:29.710
Bevel's disease may have been curable on Land.

00:27:30.700 --> 00:27:33.850
But he would've been condemned to an even harder life there!

00:27:34.630 --> 00:27:37.670
I'm sorry. I hid that from you.

00:27:37.670 --> 00:27:39.850
Leema... You're...

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:43.040
This is the Carkyness.

00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:43.800
Is Ledo there?

00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:46.220
Amy...

00:27:46.810 --> 00:27:48.420
Amy was abducted!

00:27:48.420 --> 00:27:48.930
What?!

00:27:49.140 --> 00:27:50.140
What was that?!

00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:52.350
Two men grabbed her out of nowhere!

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:54.440
How dare they?

00:27:55.380 --> 00:27:56.700
What should we do, Ledo?!

00:27:56.700 --> 00:27:57.490
Where?

00:27:57.490 --> 00:27:59.150
Near the dining hall
we went to the other day!

00:27:59.470 --> 00:28:00.290
I'll be right there!

00:28:00.290 --> 00:28:01.350
Wait!

00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:03.260
Those two work for me.

00:28:03.260 --> 00:28:04.530
They're after you!

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:05.200
What?!

00:28:05.730 --> 00:28:07.730
Amy is a hostage.

00:28:07.730 --> 00:28:10.080
If they capture you too,
you'll never be able to get back!

00:28:10.850 --> 00:28:13.000
I'll convince them to let me take her back!

00:28:13.910 --> 00:28:14.630
What?

00:28:15.140 --> 00:28:16.040
Ledo!

00:28:17.180 --> 00:28:19.050
Send an emergency call to the Oceanus!

00:28:19.700 --> 00:28:20.750
Amy?!

00:28:28.030 --> 00:28:31.020
Damn it! Untie me!

00:28:33.580 --> 00:28:35.360
You're a feisty one, aren't you?

00:28:47.490 --> 00:28:48.450
This is Leema!

00:28:48.930 --> 00:28:50.660
Release the hostage immediately!

00:28:51.530 --> 00:28:52.830
Can't do that.

00:28:52.830 --> 00:28:55.070
Right now, she's our lifeline.

00:28:55.880 --> 00:29:01.010
I'm sure the target would do anything when this girl's life is on the line.

00:29:01.010 --> 00:29:02.490
What are you talking about?!

00:29:02.490 --> 00:29:06.480
The second the armada showed itself,
it was too late.

00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:07.600
The mission has been canceled!

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.850
Why can't you understand that?!

00:29:10.130 --> 00:29:14.350
Unlike you, we're set on carrying out our duty.

00:29:14.350 --> 00:29:15.400
Wait!

00:29:18.310 --> 00:29:18.990
Leema!

00:29:19.830 --> 00:29:21.280
Ledo! How?!

00:29:44.280 --> 00:29:46.370
I was right! That's no Yunboro!

00:29:46.370 --> 00:29:48.510
Leema, what the hell is that?!

00:29:49.460 --> 00:29:52.810
We call it an Augmented Body.

00:29:52.810 --> 00:29:54.560
His name is Muzzle.

00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:56.040
ls one of your comrades inside?

00:29:56.040 --> 00:29:57.410
No one's inside.

00:29:59.650 --> 00:30:00.930
But you're right.

00:30:00.930 --> 00:30:01.930
A comrade...

00:30:02.500 --> 00:30:03.650
A friend...

00:30:04.140 --> 00:30:05.620
No pilot?!

00:30:05.620 --> 00:30:06.860
It can't be...

00:30:09.550 --> 00:30:10.800
Artillery fire?!

00:30:12.930 --> 00:30:13.540
Incoming message!

00:30:15.170 --> 00:30:19.590
Our armada's objective is to wipe out the vessels that have broken away from your fleet,

00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:22.830
including the personnel and equipment aboard.

00:30:22.830 --> 00:30:25.970
Those ships belong to our country.

00:30:25.970 --> 00:30:28.470
Please refrain from interfering.

00:30:29.200 --> 00:30:30.730
I cannot accept!

00:30:30.730 --> 00:30:35.170
Residents of this fleet are aboard both vessels.

00:30:35.170 --> 00:30:36.640
Withdraw your attack!

00:30:37.950 --> 00:30:41.220
We are exercising the legitimate, sovereign right of our country.

00:30:41.220 --> 00:30:44.780
Your fleet is already within range of our guns.

00:30:45.580 --> 00:30:46.640
What?!

00:30:46.640 --> 00:30:49.740
Interfere, and we will use our full force to eliminate you.

00:30:51.620 --> 00:30:52.490
Commodore...

00:30:52.920 --> 00:30:54.010
Yes.

00:30:54.010 --> 00:30:57.870
I cannot overlook the mention
of any harm coming to our people.

00:30:58.920 --> 00:31:00.650
All ships, prepare to attack!

00:31:00.650 --> 00:31:02.060
Shore up defenses!

00:31:02.060 --> 00:31:04.560
Escort ships, move out!

00:31:24.090 --> 00:31:25.110
Ledo!

00:31:25.110 --> 00:31:26.030
Come aboard!

00:31:26.480 --> 00:31:29.650
No matter what happens to me,
I have to protect you!

00:31:29.650 --> 00:31:30.780
For Amy's sake!

00:31:31.050 --> 00:31:32.470
What do you mean?

00:31:32.470 --> 00:31:33.570
Just who are you?!

00:31:34.090 --> 00:31:40.960
I was trying to involve you in the centuries-long conflict between nations on Land.

00:31:41.520 --> 00:31:44.840
I tried to use you for our own gain!

00:31:47.420 --> 00:31:49.320
But I can't do it anymore.

00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:52.390
We don't have the right
to destroy your way of life.

00:31:53.080 --> 00:31:54.100
Leema...

00:31:54.430 --> 00:31:55.300
Get on!

00:32:11.240 --> 00:32:14.600
All noncombatants,
evacuate to the fleet's port side!

00:32:14.600 --> 00:32:18.500
I repeat, all noncombatants,
evacuate to the fleet's port side!

00:32:19.120 --> 00:32:21.210
Please do not panic!

00:32:20.200 --> 00:32:21.210
Quit shoving!

00:32:21.210 --> 00:32:23.670
Please cross over to the port side!

00:32:21.610 --> 00:32:23.010
I said, quit shoving!

00:32:23.670 --> 00:32:27.340
Please let children and the elderly go first!

00:32:27.680 --> 00:32:28.710
That's...

00:32:29.970 --> 00:32:32.460
The enemy is outside our range of fire.

00:32:32.460 --> 00:32:34.300
Stay on guard while pushing ahead!

00:32:37.930 --> 00:32:40.710
Confirmed! The enemy's
heavy warship opened fire!

00:32:40.710 --> 00:32:42.770
All escort ships, hold your fire!

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:49.460
Impact confirmed!

00:32:49.460 --> 00:32:51.030
They've gauged our distance!

00:32:51.030 --> 00:32:52.220
They're coming!

00:32:52.220 --> 00:32:53.200
Then I have no choice.

00:32:53.850 --> 00:32:56.160
Escort ships, you have permission to return fire!

00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:12.420
It'll be all right. Okay?

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:17.010
I hope Amy's okay...

00:33:17.430 --> 00:33:18.660
Where're you going?

00:33:18.660 --> 00:33:20.060
We're supposed to evacuate!

00:33:20.590 --> 00:33:21.600
Hey!

00:33:26.050 --> 00:33:29.520
Oh, my. Were you worried about me?

00:33:31.110 --> 00:33:32.900
Adios, Pinion.

00:33:32.900 --> 00:33:35.240
I won't forget you.

00:33:40.490 --> 00:33:42.390
Uh... Hey...

00:33:47.390 --> 00:33:48.540
Don't tell me...

00:33:50.740 --> 00:33:51.920
Boss!

00:33:51.920 --> 00:33:53.970
Good work gathering intelligence!

00:33:54.780 --> 00:33:57.400
Thanks to that, I've made up my mind.

00:33:57.400 --> 00:33:59.180
Now, let's go!

00:34:17.400 --> 00:34:18.490
This is...

00:34:18.920 --> 00:34:20.020
What is it?

00:34:20.020 --> 00:34:21.700
I've never seen one before.

00:34:22.440 --> 00:34:25.120
This is enhancing the control system?!

00:34:34.690 --> 00:34:36.050
I don't believe it!

00:34:36.050 --> 00:34:38.050
This has never happened before!

00:34:38.050 --> 00:34:39.040
You can make it move?

00:34:39.540 --> 00:34:40.260
Ledo?

00:34:42.910 --> 00:34:44.370
Picture it moving.

00:34:44.970 --> 00:34:46.970
Visualize how you want it to move.

00:34:46.970 --> 00:34:49.060
How <i>you</i> want to move!

00:34:49.600 --> 00:34:52.650
If it works along the same lines as Chamber, it should be able to read your mind.

00:34:59.910 --> 00:35:00.910
Jump over there!

00:35:59.980 --> 00:36:01.110
Rackage!

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:07.010
We're closing up shop as bodyguards.

00:36:08.350 --> 00:36:11.050
It's back to the pirate trade for us.

00:36:12.140 --> 00:36:16.070
Right now, I don't want to aggravate the situation with Land.

00:36:17.220 --> 00:36:19.900
But just this once, we're not going to stand on ceremony!

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:22.150
Let's say goodbye by cutting loose!

00:36:22.410 --> 00:36:23.360
Aye, sir!

00:36:28.000 --> 00:36:30.000
Rest when you're dead! Keep firing!

00:36:47.440 --> 00:36:48.600
An electromagnetic weapon?

00:37:17.590 --> 00:37:18.460
Amy!

00:37:19.610 --> 00:37:20.380
Ledo!

00:37:26.370 --> 00:37:27.180
Amy!

00:37:27.500 --> 00:37:28.380
Ledo!

00:37:28.380 --> 00:37:28.890
Hold on!

00:37:31.230 --> 00:37:32.290
Ledo!

00:37:32.290 --> 00:37:33.130
Amy...

00:37:33.130 --> 00:37:34.060
You're not hurt?!

00:37:34.430 --> 00:37:35.250
No.

00:37:35.250 --> 00:37:37.210
Ledo, you came to get me...

00:37:42.080 --> 00:37:43.490
They're aiming at me?

00:37:44.120 --> 00:37:47.870
I'm going to sink that mech
before it falls into enemy hands.

00:37:47.870 --> 00:37:49.410
And you with it, of course.

00:37:51.930 --> 00:37:53.830
Amy, you're safe!

00:37:55.400 --> 00:37:56.410
I have to get away!

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:00.940
Leema!

00:38:01.720 --> 00:38:03.700
She's piloting it!

00:38:03.700 --> 00:38:04.510
l don't believe it...

00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:15.020
I guess I'm not as good at this as Ledo.

00:38:21.550 --> 00:38:23.780
Am I right? Or not?

00:38:24.220 --> 00:38:24.940
Which is it?

00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:34.080
Picture it...

00:39:40.540 --> 00:39:42.400
Maybe it's better this way.

00:39:42.400 --> 00:39:45.480
You were an amazing mech.

00:39:53.290 --> 00:39:56.550
If there were several others like you that could be used,

00:39:56.550 --> 00:39:58.400
everything would be messed up.

00:39:59.000 --> 00:40:00.390
Never mind a war.

00:40:00.390 --> 00:40:02.690
Every place with living beings would be destroyed.

00:40:03.570 --> 00:40:04.550
I'm sorry.

00:40:05.050 --> 00:40:08.960
l should have returned you
to the bottom of the sea earlier.

00:40:28.620 --> 00:40:31.860
L-Leema...

00:41:42.020 --> 00:41:43.020
Muzzle...

00:41:44.510 --> 00:41:47.200
Muzzle... System...

00:41:47.700 --> 00:41:48.520
You...

00:41:48.920 --> 00:41:50.290
You can speak?

00:41:50.290 --> 00:41:52.500
...Interface.

00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:53.620
Me.

00:41:55.440 --> 00:41:56.980
Yes...

00:41:56.980 --> 00:41:58.090
Yes!

00:41:58.710 --> 00:42:00.360
You're Muzzle!

00:42:00.360 --> 00:42:01.400
I'm...

00:42:01.930 --> 00:42:02.870
Leema.

00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:06.650
My... pilot.

00:42:10.420 --> 00:42:11.350
Muzzle!

00:42:14.550 --> 00:42:17.060
My... friend.

00:42:37.530 --> 00:42:38.490
Muzzle!

00:42:38.490 --> 00:42:39.120
Wait!

00:42:39.120 --> 00:42:39.660
What are you—

00:42:45.120 --> 00:42:46.000
Muzzle!

00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:47.410
Hey, wait!

00:42:53.530 --> 00:42:56.190
Muzzle!

00:43:20.150 --> 00:43:21.410
Oh, no...

00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:26.500
No, look!

00:43:34.670 --> 00:43:36.010
Leema!

00:43:37.450 --> 00:43:38.130
Leema!

00:43:38.130 --> 00:43:39.210
Thank goodness!

00:43:39.210 --> 00:43:40.010
You're not hurt!

00:43:40.010 --> 00:43:40.920
Stay there!

00:43:40.920 --> 00:43:41.980
I'll get help!

00:43:41.980 --> 00:43:43.190
No need.

00:43:43.820 --> 00:43:45.640
I can't go back to Gargantia.

00:43:45.640 --> 00:43:46.850
What do you mean?!

00:43:47.780 --> 00:43:50.890
None of this would've happened if it weren't for me.

00:43:50.890 --> 00:43:52.880
That sin won't go away.

00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:54.160
That doesn't matter!

00:43:54.160 --> 00:43:56.210
This isn't the time to be thinking about that!

00:43:57.220 --> 00:43:59.760
Muzzle was all I had.

00:43:59.760 --> 00:44:01.940
But now he's gone.

00:44:01.940 --> 00:44:04.010
I have nowhere to go home to.

00:44:05.240 --> 00:44:07.260
It sounds like you're in a bind.

00:44:07.750 --> 00:44:10.880
Your life was saved, but now you don't know what to do with it.

00:44:14.350 --> 00:44:15.440
Rackage!

00:44:15.440 --> 00:44:16.920
Bring Leema back here!

00:44:18.860 --> 00:44:21.040
I must say farewell now.

00:44:21.040 --> 00:44:22.130
A thousand pardons.

00:44:22.850 --> 00:44:24.060
Rackage...

00:44:26.530 --> 00:44:27.980
Those eyes.

00:44:27.980 --> 00:44:31.100
Those are the eyes of someone
for whom living has become a curse.

00:44:31.100 --> 00:44:32.440
They're lovely.

00:44:38.130 --> 00:44:41.520
Well, come with me.

00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:43.990
That is, if you dare.

00:44:57.330 --> 00:44:59.350
Ledo, Amy...

00:44:59.860 --> 00:45:02.130
Please allow me to atone this way.

00:45:02.420 --> 00:45:03.590
Leema!

00:45:07.570 --> 00:45:09.290
Don't worry.

00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:11.490
There is only one sea.

00:45:21.740 --> 00:45:22.800
Leema...

00:45:51.330 --> 00:45:52.060
To all fleet members.

00:45:53.260 --> 00:45:57.520
Thank you for your hard work
during this long period of repairs.

00:45:58.260 --> 00:46:03.990
As of this moment, Gargantia can count one more fortress amongst her forces.

00:46:05.340 --> 00:46:11.900
We believe the unknown enemy from before was the naval force of a Land nation.

00:46:12.640 --> 00:46:14.660
But thanks to the escort fleet's strenuous efforts

00:46:14.660 --> 00:46:19.000
and your own cooperation,
the damage was kept to a minimum.

00:46:20.740 --> 00:46:28.000
As we meet new ships going forth,
Gargantia must remain a peaceful, abundant fleet.

00:46:28.830 --> 00:46:31.930
Please lend me your efforts toward that end.

00:46:39.730 --> 00:46:40.650
That mech...

00:46:41.420 --> 00:46:43.110
definitely linked with this.

00:46:43.930 --> 00:46:47.190
There are still things on Earth that I know nothing about.

00:46:47.690 --> 00:46:48.700
Ledo...

00:46:49.300 --> 00:46:52.460
Leema was born in a nation on Land
that's perpetually at war.

00:46:52.460 --> 00:46:55.160
I wonder what her life was like
before she came here.

00:46:55.160 --> 00:46:58.520
I wonder how she felt
when she looked at us.

00:46:58.520 --> 00:46:59.510
I don't know.

00:47:00.220 --> 00:47:05.510
But Leema said she didn't want to destroy our way of life.

00:47:07.610 --> 00:47:11.720
We're going to live here,
no matter what troubles we face.

00:47:16.950 --> 00:47:19.350
I'm going to protect you here.

00:47:21.550 --> 00:47:22.400
Ledo...

00:48:09.180 --> 00:48:15.930
kore made wa betsu no michi ayundekita futari

00:48:09.180 --> 00:48:15.930
We used to walk different paths

00:48:15.930 --> 00:48:21.940
onaji jikan wo kizamihajimeta n da

00:48:15.930 --> 00:48:21.940
Now our time together has begun

00:48:21.940 --> 00:48:28.570
taisetsu na takaramono katachi wa mienai kedo

00:48:21.940 --> 00:48:28.570
The truly important things are invisible to the eye

00:48:28.570 --> 00:48:34.930
te wo tsunaidara fureta ki ga shita

00:48:28.570 --> 00:48:34.930
I think I know what matters when I touch your hand

00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:41.100
kimi no hitomi ni utsuru atarashii keshiki

00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:41.100
I want to know what the future will be like

00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:49.570
dare yori chikaku de watashi mo issho ni mitsumetai

00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:49.570
I want to hear it directly from you

00:48:49.570 --> 00:48:55.840
oboeteite ne itsumo soba ni iru yo

00:48:49.570 --> 00:48:55.840
Remember, I'm right here

00:48:55.840 --> 00:49:02.150
kore kara mo kimi ga kaeru basho de itai kara

00:48:55.840 --> 00:49:02.150
I want to be there when you return

00:49:02.150 --> 00:49:09.450
kimi no tonari de zutto warattetai yo

00:49:02.150 --> 00:49:09.450
I want to laugh beside you

00:49:09.450 --> 00:49:17.920
futari no chizu wo kasaneawasete susumou

00:49:09.450 --> 00:49:17.920
Let us sail together

